Usages:
  functional_options: |
    Get/Put/Delete/Watch calls take a base set of positional arguments plus a variadic list of
    OpOption functional-options (WithPrefix, WithRev, WithLease, WithSort, WithLimit, ...) that
    mutate a shared Op builder before the request is sent. Prefer adding a new OpOption over
    adding a new positional parameter or a new top-level method when extending request shaping.

Annotations: |
  This cell is etcd's public Go client API: a thin gRPC-stub wrapper around the wire protocol
  served by the server-side gRPC adapter cell. It is the package etcdctl and every external Go
  consumer of etcd links against. It has no dependency on any other cell documented in this
  forest — it talks to the server exclusively over the network (gRPC), not through a shared Go
  import — making it a genuine external-facing leaf.

  Use `functional_options` when a new request needs additional optional shaping parameters.

---

"Client(configuration Config)":
  location: client.go
  annotations: |
    Owns one gRPC connection to an etcd cluster (via a manual endpoint resolver for
    load-balancing across the configured endpoints) plus the six sub-clients below,
    constructed from that connection.

    `configuration`: dial targets, TLS, timeouts, and credentials.
  properties:
    "Username -> string": |
      Username used for password-based authentication, if configured.
    "Password -> string": |
      Password used for password-based authentication, if configured.
  methods:
    "Close() -> err:error": |
      Close the underlying gRPC connection and release resources.
    "Endpoints() -> endpoints:[]string": |
      Currently configured server endpoints.
    "Sync() -> err:error": |
      Refresh the endpoint list from the cluster's current member list.

"KV()":
  location: kv.go
  annotations: |
    Key/value read and write operations, translated 1:1 into the corresponding protobuf
    request/response pair.
  methods:
    "Put(key string, value string) -> response:PutResponse, err:error": |
      Create or overwrite the value at `key`.
    "Get(key string) -> response:GetResponse, err:error": |
      Fetch the value(s) at `key` (or a range, with `functional_options`).
    "Delete(key string) -> response:DeleteResponse, err:error": |
      Delete the value(s) at `key` (or a range, with `functional_options`).
    "Compact(revision int64) -> response:CompactResponse, err:error": |
      Discard all revisions of all keys created before `revision`.
    "Txn() -> transaction:Txn": |
      Begin a new conditional mini-transaction.

"Lease()":
  location: lease.go
  annotations: |
    Grants, revokes, and renews TTL-based leases; a thin client-side mirror of the server-side
    lease cell's lessor contract.
  methods:
    "Grant(ttlSeconds int64) -> response:LeaseGrantResponse, err:error": |
      Request a new lease that expires after at least `ttlSeconds`.
    "Revoke(id int64) -> response:LeaseRevokeResponse, err:error": |
      Revoke a lease immediately, deleting every key attached to it.
    "TimeToLive(id int64) -> response:LeaseTimeToLiveResponse, err:error": |
      Query a lease's remaining TTL and, optionally, its attached keys.
    "KeepAliveOnce(id int64) -> response:LeaseKeepAliveResponse, err:error": |
      Send a single keep-alive heartbeat for a lease, resetting its TTL countdown.

"Watcher()":
  location: watch.go
  annotations: |
    Subscribes to a stream of key-change events for a key or range, starting at an optional
    historical revision.
  methods:
    "Watch(key string) -> events:WatchStream": |
      Begin watching `key` (or a range, with `functional_options`). Delivered as a
      receive-only stream of change-event response values in the real implementation.
    "RequestProgress() -> err:error": |
      Ask the server to emit a progress notification even if no matching events have occurred
      recently.
    "Close() -> err:error": |
      Stop all watches created through this `Watcher` and release its resources.

"Txn()":
  location: txn.go
  annotations: |
    A conditional mini-transaction: evaluate comparisons, then run one of two operation lists
    depending on the result.
  methods:
    "If(comparisons []Comparison) -> transaction:Txn": |
      Set the comparisons that determine which branch executes.
    "Then(operations []Operation) -> transaction:Txn": |
      Set the operations to run if every previously-set comparison succeeds.
    "Else(operations []Operation) -> transaction:Txn": |
      Set the operations to run if any previously-set comparison fails.
    "Commit() -> response:TxnResponse, err:error": |
      Evaluate the comparisons and execute the chosen branch atomically.

